# L set, kernel 32. Parker, Zavalishin and Le Bivic, DAFx-16, Fig. 11: Moog-ladder-like filter, input minus k times the
# output, a tanh, then four one-pole lowpasses, k = 3 (their Fig. 13). Here the feedback carries a unit delay (no
# Newton solve, no antialiasing), the one-poles are y += g (x - y) at 2 kHz (g = 0.230329), and tanh is replaced by
# Yeh, Abel and Smith eq. (19), n = 2.5.
state float y1 = 0
state float y2 = 0
state float y3 = 0
state float y4 = 0
u = in * 2.0 - 3.0 * y4
t = u / ((1.0 + (abs(u) ^ 2.5)) ^ 0.4)
y1 = y1 + 0.230329 * (t - y1)
y2 = y2 + 0.230329 * (y1 - y2)
y3 = y3 + 0.230329 * (y2 - y3)
y4 = y4 + 0.230329 * (y3 - y4)
out = y4 * 0.8
